  "nl_text": "The rschema_0480 database is designed to manage information about properties, agents, users, and their responsibilities. The Property table stores details about individual properties, including their address, built area, construction year, whether they are apartments, a unique property ID, property certificate, photos, sale price, and sales status. The Agent table contains information about real estate agents, such as their ID, contact number, home address, and name. The User table holds data about users, including their password, role, unique user ID, and username. The Responsibility table links agents to properties, indicating the start and end times of their responsibilities, and it ensures that each agent is associated with at least one property and vice versa through a composite primary key and foreign keys referencing the Agent and Property tables, with the Agent_ID referencing the Agent table and Property_ID referencing the Property table, and both Agent_ID and Property_ID are not nullable, enforcing referential integrity.",
  "gold_question": "This is a real estate information management system. For property management, the system records basic information for each property, including unique property ID, property certificate, address, construction year, built area, sale price, property photos and sales status (for sale, sold, off market), with additional apartment-specific information required for apartment-type properties. For real estate agent management, the system records basic information for each agent, including unique agent ID, name, home address and contact number. Each property can only be managed by one agent at a time, and the system needs to record the responsibility period (start time, end time). For user management, the system records basic information for each user, including unique user ID, username, password and role (real estate agent or system administrator). Users need to pass authentication before logging into the system. After logging in, real estate agents can enter information for properties they are responsible for selling, but this requires system administrator approval and authorization. All users can query property information, while system administrators can also export property information lists and periodically organize sales status, removing properties that are no longer for sale from the system.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0480.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0480\nCREATE TABLE `property` (\n  `property_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `built_area` float NOT NULL,\n  `construction_year` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `is_apartment` tinyint(1) NOT NULL,\n  `property_certificate` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `photos` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  `sale_price` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `sales_status` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`property_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `agent` (\n  `agent_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `contact_number` varchar(20) NOT NULL,\n  `home_address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`agent_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `user` (\n  `user_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `username` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `role` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`user_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `responsibility` (\n  `agent_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `property_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`agent_id`, `property_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `responsibility_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`agent_id`) REFERENCES `agent` (`agent_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `responsibility_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`property_id`) REFERENCES `property` (`property_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
